WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:02.501
I want to read a part
of a letter that you posted

00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:05.876
on your Instagram account
in December, 2020, okay?

00:00:05.918 --> 00:00:08.542
- Yeah.
- And you wrote...

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:45.501
So can you describe the weeks
and the months

00:00:45.542 --> 00:00:46.709
and maybe even the years

00:00:46.751 --> 00:00:49.209
that led up to you
posting that letter.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.834
What were the factors
that helped you make

00:00:51.876 --> 00:00:55.542
that monumental decision?

00:00:55.584 --> 00:00:59.542
Goodness. Um, I mean,
definitely, uh,

00:00:59.584 --> 00:01:01.667
obviously quite the journey.

00:01:01.709 --> 00:01:05.792
I'd say leading up to it
and the months before,

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:10.292
what I really had was a moment
for myself, um,

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:14.459
where-- and this is obviously
quite a privileged thing to say,

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:20.417
but I wasn't working, um,
because of the current situation

00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:24.209
we're in with the pandemic,
and I was up in Nova Scotia,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.542
and I spent a lot of time
just by myself.

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:32.667
Um, and I think it really
allowed me sort of

00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:37.542
separating from, you know,
that world, so to speak, uh,

00:01:37.584 --> 00:01:42.959
for a moment, um,
to really get to

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.417
sit with myself and certain,
um, aspects

00:01:48.459 --> 00:01:52.292
that I had never given myself
the opportunity to do,

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:56.209
and I think that was definitely
on purpose to a degree.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.751
Even though I wasn't
necessarily aware of it,

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:04.417
just, you know, avoiding so much
in a way.

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:09.501
The busyness of life allowed
and has allowed most people

00:02:09.542 --> 00:02:11.375
to not to look inward.

00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:14.751
And so what you're sharing is
is that you had this time alone

00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:16.501
in No-- were--
were you physically alone?

00:02:16.542 --> 00:02:19.626
I was pretty alone
in Nova Scotia, yeah, like--

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.501
- Okay.
- I mean, seeing people,

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.167
of course, too, but really
purposefully was--

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:29.250
it was probably the first time
in my life

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:32.584
where I really felt okay
and comfortable alone.

00:02:32.626 --> 00:02:36.125
It used to just be
incredibly difficult for me

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:39.250
to even just sort of sit
with myself.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:43.125
Um, and this was a time
where that was possible

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:48.667
and really, uh, relax
and let my body relax.

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:50.709
I think I realized getting
to that space

00:02:50.751 --> 00:02:53.250
and getting surrounded
by nature more...

00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:55.209
- Yeah.
- It almost was like steps

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.834
into relaxation.
It was like I would notice

00:02:57.876 --> 00:03:01.834
my body sort of go into that
space more and more.

00:03:01.876 --> 00:03:04.792
And I think on some level,
it probably allowed me

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:09.209
to connect to my body
in a way that I--

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.626
I could really fully listen
to myself.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:15.042
And I think for so long I...

00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:18.501
didn't even have a concept
of what I was feeling, you know?

